---
import MainLayout from '@/layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import LegalFooter from '@/components/LegalFooter.astro';
import {
  LEGAL_OPERATOR_LOCATION,
  LEGAL_OPERATOR_NAME,
  TRADING_NAME,
} from '@/lib/legal/businessIdentity';
import { SAAS_EXPORT_RETENTION_DAYS } from '@/lib/setup/saasEntitlement';
import { PAGE_DESCRIPTIONS } from '@/lib/seo/defaults';
import '@/styles/legal-pages.css';
---

<MainLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Kersivo"
  description={PAGE_DESCRIPTIONS.privacy}
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <main class="legal-page">
    <article class="container legal-page__inner">
      <h1 class="legal-page__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-page__updated">Last updated: 21 September 2026</p>

      <p>
        This policy describes how personal data is processed when you use websites and services operated under the
        KERSIVO brand for UK barbershops, including marketing pages, live product preview booking and shop flows,
        monthly subscription checkout, and (where applicable) the barbershop admin experience. It is written in plain
        language and does not replace legal advice.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Note:</strong> The live public offer is a £39/month subscription with no setup fee. References below to
        a &ldquo;setup deposit&rdquo; describe a gated legacy checkout path that is not currently offered publicly; if
        that path is re-enabled, the same payment-related processing rules apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is responsible for your data?</h2>
      <p>
        The legal operator of the {TRADING_NAME} service is <strong>{LEGAL_OPERATOR_NAME}</strong>, trading as
        {TRADING_NAME}, based in {LEGAL_OPERATOR_LOCATION}. References in this policy to &ldquo;{TRADING_NAME}&rdquo;,
        &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo; and &ldquo;our&rdquo; mean {LEGAL_OPERATOR_NAME} trading as {TRADING_NAME},
        unless the context refers specifically to a barbershop using the service.
      </p>
      <p>
        {TRADING_NAME} is <strong>not</strong> the controller for every category of personal data processed through the
        platform. Roles depend on whose relationship with the data subject is involved.
      </p>

      <h3>When the barbershop is the controller</h3>
      <p>
        Where a live barbershop uses {TRADING_NAME} to run its own booking, client records, notes, retail pickup, staff
        roster or related operational tools, that <strong>barbershop determines the purposes and means</strong> of
        processing personal data about its customers, clients, barbers and team members. In those cases, the barbershop
        is the <strong>data controller</strong>, and {TRADING_NAME} processes that personal data
        <strong>on the barbershop&rsquo;s behalf</strong> as a <strong>processor</strong> to provide the software
        service (for example hosting bookings, sending transactional confirmations or reminders, and storing client CRM
        records).
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are a customer of a barbershop that uses {TRADING_NAME}, you should normally contact that barbershop first
        about your personal data. {TRADING_NAME} can assist the barbershop where appropriate. The contractual terms for
        {TRADING_NAME}&rsquo;s processor role with business Clients are set out in the
        <a href="/dpa">Data Processing Agreement</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>When {TRADING_NAME} is an independent controller</h3>
      <p>
        {TRADING_NAME} remains an <strong>independent controller</strong> for personal data it processes for its own
        business purposes, including:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>{TRADING_NAME} account-holder details and authentication / security records;</li>
        <li>subscription and billing administration;</li>
        <li>terms acceptance and related contract records;</li>
        <li>support and contact enquiries sent directly to {TRADING_NAME};</li>
        <li>direct communications between {TRADING_NAME} and the business customer (the barbershop);</li>
        <li>tax, accounting and legal records {TRADING_NAME} must keep;</li>
        <li>consented analytics and advertising measurement on {TRADING_NAME} marketing pages;</li>
        <li>fraud, security and abuse-prevention records; and</li>
        <li>{TRADING_NAME} operational audit records.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        For data protection enquiries about {TRADING_NAME}&rsquo;s own controller processing, or to exercise rights
        relating to that data, contact:
        <a href="mailto:hello@kersivo.co.uk">hello@kersivo.co.uk</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What data we process and why</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you interact with us, we may process:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact and setup enquiries</strong> — name, email address and message content you submit through our
          contact form. <strong>Purpose:</strong> responding to your request. <strong>Legal basis (UK):</strong>
          legitimate interests. ({TRADING_NAME} as independent controller.)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Setup deposits</strong> — name, email, shop details and payment status when you pay a KERSIVO setup
          deposit via Stripe Checkout on our account. <strong>Purpose:</strong> taking payment, confirming the deposit,
          sending onboarding information and internal fulfilment notices.
          <strong>Legal basis (UK):</strong> performance of a contract / steps prior to a contract.
          ({TRADING_NAME} as independent controller.)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Campaign attribution on checkout</strong> — if present in the page URL when you start checkout, we may
          pass advertising or campaign identifiers (for example gclid, gbraid, wbraid or UTM parameters) into Stripe
          session metadata and include a summary in internal fulfilment email. We do not store these identifiers in
          browser cookies or local storage before you choose optional advertising measurement in our cookie banner.
          <strong>Purpose:</strong> understanding which campaigns relate to setup purchases.
          <strong>Legal basis (UK):</strong> requires confirmation with our legal adviser (typically legitimate interests
          and/or consent for related storage technologies — see the Cookie Policy).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Booking data (live barbershop)</strong> — service, barber, date/time, and contact details (name and
          email; phone if provided). Processed so the barbershop can manage appointments, confirmations, reschedule and
          cancel links, and related emails. On a live tenant site the <strong>barbershop is the controller</strong>;
          {TRADING_NAME} processes this data as <strong>processor</strong>. Demo / sandbox booking flows on the
          marketing site are simulations or previews and are described separately where they apply.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Shop orders (buy-and-collect)</strong> — for a <strong>live</strong> barbershop shop: email address
          used at checkout, order contents, payment status as recorded after payment, and related confirmation emails to
          fulfil your purchase. Card payments are handled securely by <strong>Stripe</strong> on the
          <strong>barbershop&rsquo;s own Stripe account</strong>; we do not store full card numbers on our servers. The
          barbershop is typically the controller of retail customer data; {TRADING_NAME} processes it as processor to
          run the shop software. The public retail demo on this marketing site is a simulation only and does not collect
          checkout personal data, take payment, or create an order. Private owner test orders in admin may create marked
          test records without payment.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Post-purchase setup</strong> — after a KERSIVO subscription purchase, information you submit in the
          authenticated KERSIVO client onboarding (for example business details, branding, team, services, opening hours,
          photos and migration notes) is processed to prepare your barbershop for launch.
          ({TRADING_NAME} as independent controller for the business-customer relationship; some fields may also relate
          to staff or migration content controlled by the barbershop once live.)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Admin access</strong> — first-party session cookies / tokens that keep you signed in to the
          barbershop admin panel (typically for up to 30 days), and operational logs needed for security.
          ({TRADING_NAME} as independent controller for account security.)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Content you upload</strong> — for example barber or product images where the product allows uploads.
          Stored so the site and shop can display them. Client-note images on a live shop are processed for the
          barbershop as controller.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email delivery</strong> — we use <strong>Resend</strong> to send transactional emails (for example
          booking confirmations, order confirmations, setup deposit confirmations, and contact form delivery to our
          inbox), using the addresses involved in each message. Booking and retail customer emails for a live shop are
          sent as processor on the barbershop&rsquo;s behalf; {TRADING_NAME} account and marketing emails are
          {TRADING_NAME}&rsquo;s own controller processing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Website analytics (optional)</strong> — if you accept analytics cookies on {TRADING_NAME} marketing
          pages, Google Analytics 4 may process pseudonymous usage data (for example pages viewed and approximate
          location derived by Google) to help us understand site performance. Live barbershop booking and storefront
          pages do not load {TRADING_NAME} marketing analytics tags.
          <strong>Legal basis (UK):</strong> consent. ({TRADING_NAME} as independent controller.)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Advertising measurement (optional)</strong> — if you accept advertising measurement on
          {TRADING_NAME} marketing pages, Google Ads measurement tags may process data needed to measure whether ads
          lead to enquiries or subscriptions. We do <strong>not</strong> use Google Ads Enhanced Conversions (we do not
          send hashed customer emails or phone numbers to Google). <strong>Legal basis (UK):</strong> consent.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Personalised advertising (optional)</strong> — asked for separately from measurement and off unless you
          switch it on. If you accept it, Google may add you to our remarketing audiences so we can show KERSIVO ads to
          people who have already visited the site. Withdrawing it stops future audience collection.
          <strong>Legal basis (UK):</strong> consent.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>SMS (optional)</strong> — if you subscribe to a plan that includes SMS and we enable it for your shop,
          we may process mobile numbers and message content needed to send appointment reminders through a third-party
          SMS provider, only where that feature is enabled. For live-shop reminders the barbershop is the controller and
          {TRADING_NAME} acts as processor.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Recipients and providers</h2>
      <p>
        To provide the live barbershop service, {TRADING_NAME} uses infrastructure providers that may process Customer
        Personal Data as <strong>sub-processors</strong> (on {TRADING_NAME}&rsquo;s behalf as processor for the
        barbershop), including:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Vercel</strong> — application hosting;</li>
        <li><strong>Neon</strong> / <strong>PostgreSQL</strong> — database hosting;</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> — transactional email delivery;</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Twilio</strong> — SMS delivery, only where SMS reminders are enabled for a shop.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>Other providers are used in specific functional contexts and are not listed above as general sub-processors:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Stripe</strong> — payment processing for {TRADING_NAME} subscriptions on our platform account, and for
          live barbershop deposits/retail through the barbershop&rsquo;s own Stripe Connect account at go-live (the
          barbershop remains seller of record for those shop payments). The public retail demo does not use Stripe
          Checkout. Card numbers are not stored on {TRADING_NAME} servers.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Analytics 4 / Google Ads</strong> — optional measurement on {TRADING_NAME} marketing pages
          only when you consent (see the Cookie Policy). These tags are not used on live barbershop booking or
          storefront pages.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal data. Where we engage providers to process Customer Personal Data on a barbershop&rsquo;s
        behalf, we do so under appropriate arrangements required by UK data protection law.
      </p>

      <h2>International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Data may be processed by providers outside the UK (for example in the United States). Where that happens, we
        rely on approved safeguard mechanisms required by UK data protection law (for example the UK International Data
        Transfer Agreement / Addendum or Standard Contractual Clauses), as offered by those providers. Details of each
        provider&rsquo;s transfer mechanism should be confirmed in their current data processing terms.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
      <p>
        Retention depends on whose data it is and why it is held.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Live barbershop (Customer Personal Data).</strong> While a subscription is active, shop data is kept
          to run the service. After a subscription ends, the barbershop may export a free CSV of client contact details
          and booking history for up to <strong>{SAAS_EXPORT_RETENTION_DAYS} days</strong>. After that window, the live
          shop data graph is eligible to be permanently deleted from the production database. Cancellation does
          <strong>not</strong> delete shop data instantly. Residual copies may remain briefly in encrypted backups
          until those backups expire under our hosting provider&rsquo;s normal backup cycle; we do not promise
          immediate erasure from every backup replica.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>{TRADING_NAME} independent-controller records.</strong> Account, billing, tax, legal acceptance,
          security and operational audit records may be retained for as long as needed for those purposes, including
          where UK law requires longer retention of financial or legal records. That does <strong>not</strong> mean all
          personal data of every type is kept for six years.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics and advertising cookies</strong> follow the durations in our
          <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a> when you have consented.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights (UK)</h2>
      <p>Under UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018, you may have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>request access to your personal data;</li>
        <li>ask for inaccurate data to be corrected;</li>
        <li>ask for data to be erased in certain circumstances;</li>
        <li>restrict or object to processing in certain circumstances;</li>
        <li>data portability where applicable;</li>
        <li>withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If your request relates to a barbershop&rsquo;s customers or bookings, contact that barbershop first (they are
        usually the controller). For {TRADING_NAME} account, billing or marketing data, email
        <a href="mailto:hello@kersivo.co.uk">hello@kersivo.co.uk</a>. You may also complain to the UK Information
        Commissioner&rsquo;s Office (ICO):
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/">https://ico.org.uk/</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
      <p>
        We use necessary cookies and similar technologies to run the website (for example security, payments-related
        flows, forms, remembering your privacy choices, and keeping a barbershop admin signed in). With your permission
        on {TRADING_NAME} marketing pages, we also use analytics and advertising measurement technologies as described
        in our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Admin login uses necessary first-party session cookies so you can stay signed in while managing your shop. Full
        names, purposes and durations are listed in the Cookie Policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can accept, reject or change optional technologies at any time using
        <strong>Cookie settings</strong> in the website footer, or by revisiting the cookie banner when your consent
        version is updated.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We apply appropriate technical and organisational measures appropriate to the nature of the service, including
        access controls for admin areas and encrypted connections (HTTPS) for site traffic. No online service can be
        guaranteed 100% secure.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. The &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date will change when we do. We will
        notify active clients of any material changes via email. Material changes to cookie purposes may also require a
        new consent choice.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <LegalFooter />
</MainLayout>
